set the stage for future conflicts and diplomatic negotiations. Key figures in this process included French First Consul Napoleon Bonaparte and Austrian leaders who sought to stabilize their nation after a series of military setbacks. The treaty's geographic scope extended across much of Europe, emphasizing France's growing influence and the weakening of Austrian power.

